    <div class="section-label">The short answer</div>
    <h2 id="overview-h">What group health insurance costs per employee</h2>
    <div class="answer"><p class="answer-p">Across 3,500+ companies insured through Plum, half spend between roughly ₹6,000 and ₹24,000 per employee per year (PEPY) on group health insurance. A quarter spend less than ₹6,000, and a quarter spend more than ₹24,000, mostly because they cover parents or carry a higher sum insured. Where a specific company lands depends on sum insured, family definition, employee age mix, industry risk, claims history at renewal, and the add-ons chosen.</p>
<p class="answer-p">The ranges on this page are directional. A specific quote for your company will sit somewhere inside them once an insurer sees your employee data, and that number can move 20 to 40 percent either way based on the design choices discussed below.</p></div>
