<section id="what-the-top-quarter-does-differently" class="sec" aria-labelledby="what-the-top-quarter-does-differently-h"><div class="section-label">Part 4 · Policy design</div><h2 id="what-the-top-quarter-does-differently-h">What do the highest-spending companies cover?</h2><p class="section-intro"><strong>The top quarter of companies spend over ₹24,000 per employee, and most of that comes down to policy design.</strong> More than 9 in 10 top-quarter companies cover parents, carry a sum insured of ₹7.5 lakh or more, or both.</p><figure class="cmp-card">
<figcaption>Share of companies with each feature</figcaption>
<div class="cmp-legend"><span class="li"><span class="sw top"></span>Top quarter (over ₹24,000)</span><span class="li"><span class="sw rest"></span>Everyone else</span></div>
<div class="cmp-row"><div class="cmp-label">Cover parents</div>
<div class="cmp-bars"><div class="cmp-bar top" style="width:90%"><span>90%</span></div>
<div class="cmp-bar rest" style="width:11%"><span>11%</span></div></div></div><div class="cmp-row"><div class="cmp-label">Sum insured of ₹7.5 lakh or more</div>
